1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:10,000
[English subtitles are available]

2
00:00:06,510 --> 00:00:11,920
[Once, there lived a pair
of poor siblings.]

3
00:00:12,050 --> 00:00:15,660
[One year,
there was a drought in the tribe.]

4
00:00:15,750 --> 00:00:17,420
[Every household needed water.]

5
00:00:17,550 --> 00:00:23,310
[But spring water came surging out
from the two siblings' home.]

6
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:25,730
[It was a ceaseless flow.]

7
00:00:25,820 --> 00:00:28,200
[When the people found out,]

8
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:31,370
[they chased the siblings out
of their tribe with resentment.]

9
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:39,730
[The brother and sister left
without a fight.]

10
00:00:39,810 --> 00:00:42,980
[They ran and ran along the coastline.]

11
00:00:43,110 --> 00:00:47,870
[Suddenly, there was a downpour.]

12
00:00:47,950 --> 00:00:52,050
[The flood submerged the whole tribe.]

13
00:00:52,130 --> 00:00:57,190
[However, the siblings got into a boat
that they prepared and survived.]

14
00:00:57,720 --> 00:01:00,760
[Floating along with the wind,]

15
00:01:00,840 --> 00:01:05,820
[they arrived at a fertile land
called Palidaw.]

16
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:10,660
[From then on, people regarded the rain]

17
00:01:10,740 --> 00:01:13,870
[as the Creator's messenger,]

18
00:01:13,960 --> 00:01:22,180
[bringing either blessings
or misfortune to them.]

19
00:01:42,910 --> 00:01:44,180
This is strange.

20
00:01:45,240 --> 00:01:46,910
Why am I here?

21
00:01:50,740 --> 00:01:52,150
How strange.

22
00:01:56,550 --> 00:01:58,170
Where's the Comb of Memories?

23
00:02:08,030 --> 00:02:09,310
You can see me?

24
00:02:09,389 --> 00:02:10,800
Why can't I see you?

25
00:02:10,930 --> 00:02:11,860
Why can you see me?

26
00:02:11,950 --> 00:02:13,620
Why can't I see you?

27
00:02:14,320 --> 00:02:16,350
Who are you? How did you get in here?

28
00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:18,150
Who are you?

29
00:02:18,240 --> 00:02:19,560
I'm not human.

30
00:02:19,650 --> 00:02:20,880
You're not human?

31
00:02:21,010 --> 00:02:22,770
I'm not a human. I'm a Kawas!

32
00:02:25,320 --> 00:02:26,770
You're a Kawas?

33
00:02:27,650 --> 00:02:30,340
Yes, I'm a Kawas.

34
00:02:31,880 --> 00:02:33,150
I'm a form of existence.

35
00:02:33,860 --> 00:02:36,670
I exist in the mountains and the sea.

36
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:39,800
I exist in everything

37
00:02:39,930 --> 00:02:41,600
that your eyes can see.

38
00:02:45,470 --> 00:02:47,280
Is this an illusion?

39
00:02:47,370 --> 00:02:49,210
Right, I must have had too much to drink.

40
00:02:49,300 --> 00:02:51,150
I sang a song that summoned the spirits.

41
00:02:51,240 --> 00:02:53,300
That's why I'm seeing...

42
00:02:55,460 --> 00:02:56,340
You can't be a god!

43
00:02:56,470 --> 00:02:58,410
Why else would you be in such pain?

44
00:02:59,329 --> 00:03:00,210
Don't move!

45
00:03:01,180 --> 00:03:02,850
Why do you keep reaching out your hand?

46
00:03:02,940 --> 00:03:04,520
What are you trying to do?

47
00:03:04,610 --> 00:03:05,930
I'm going to get my stuff.

48
00:03:11,830 --> 00:03:13,190
Give it back.

49
00:03:36,250 --> 00:03:39,720
[He'an Ambulance Private Limited]

50
00:04:07,790 --> 00:04:11,090
[He'an Ambulance Private Limited]

51
00:04:11,710 --> 00:04:13,690
Is that me?

52
00:04:17,610 --> 00:04:19,279
Am I dead?

53
00:05:51,540 --> 00:06:02,810
[Episode 2,
Guardian Angel or Grim Reaper?]

54
00:06:03,820 --> 00:06:05,930
[Have you forgotten what you told me?]

55
00:06:06,020 --> 00:06:07,690
[That I'm the only one who can see you]

56
00:06:07,780 --> 00:06:09,710
[and feel your presence in this world.]

57
00:06:11,740 --> 00:06:12,310
[Guardian angel.]

58
00:06:12,400 --> 00:06:14,770
[You'll always be by my side, right?]

59
00:06:15,210 --> 00:06:17,850
[If it rains every day,]

60
00:06:17,940 --> 00:06:20,630
[then I'll be able]

61
00:06:22,390 --> 00:06:26,260
[to see you all the time.]

62
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:34,400
Good. Straighten your arms.

63
00:06:34,490 --> 00:06:36,200
Splash the water. Let me see the splash.

64
00:06:36,330 --> 00:06:37,560
Is there a splash?

65
00:06:37,650 --> 00:06:39,320
Okay, kick.

66
00:06:39,409 --> 00:06:40,950
Kick it up. Come on.

67
00:06:41,880 --> 00:06:42,670
Your mom is over there.

68
00:06:42,760 --> 00:06:44,300
Wave to your mom.

69
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,480
Wave to your mom.

70
00:06:45,570 --> 00:06:47,380
Okay. Show me the splash.

71
00:06:53,180 --> 00:06:54,640
Why am I here?

72
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:59,300
What happened last night?

73
00:07:01,240 --> 00:07:03,390
[It's only one drink.]

74
00:07:03,520 --> 00:07:04,800
Why are you so nervous?

75
00:07:04,930 --> 00:07:06,380
And you call yourself
Kakarayan's messenger?

76
00:07:06,470 --> 00:07:07,440
I think

77
00:07:07,530 --> 00:07:09,900
you're just His servant.

78
00:07:10,780 --> 00:07:12,320
No. You're not His servant.

79
00:07:12,410 --> 00:07:13,820
You are...

80
00:07:13,910 --> 00:07:16,640
His slave dog.

81
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,700
"I'm not 'Orad. I'm a dog.

82
00:07:18,790 --> 00:07:20,160
I can't drink it."

83
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:23,280
Nice. That's the 'Orad I know.

84
00:07:23,410 --> 00:07:24,160
No way.

85
00:07:24,250 --> 00:07:25,960
Just because I had one drink...

86
00:07:29,350 --> 00:07:31,110
What god of creation?

87
00:07:31,990 --> 00:07:33,490
He's just a typical boss.

88
00:07:34,230 --> 00:07:35,070
No.

89
00:07:37,310 --> 00:07:38,770
He's worse than a typical boss.

90
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,260
He's the most powerful in heaven.

91
00:07:40,350 --> 00:07:41,710
No one can tell Him what to do.

92
00:07:45,810 --> 00:07:46,510
'Orad.

93
00:07:47,170 --> 00:07:48,840
I think it's almost time.

94
00:07:48,970 --> 00:07:50,340
Why don't I go and buy...

95
00:07:57,730 --> 00:07:58,350
Okay.

96
00:08:00,110 --> 00:08:01,250
I'll go get another bottle.

97
00:08:05,870 --> 00:08:07,190
Then what?

98
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:09,130
After that jerk got me drunk...

99
00:08:15,420 --> 00:08:17,570
Who are you? How did you get in here?

100
00:08:17,660 --> 00:08:18,630
Who are you?

101
00:08:19,470 --> 00:08:20,350
I'm not human.

102
00:08:27,430 --> 00:08:28,130
I'm doomed.

103
00:08:46,130 --> 00:08:46,920
It's okay.

104
00:08:47,620 --> 00:08:48,370
It's okay.

105
00:08:49,520 --> 00:08:50,570
It was a dream.

106
00:09:06,460 --> 00:09:09,760
Was what happened yesterday real?

107
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,340
Was it real?

108
00:09:14,900 --> 00:09:16,660
Is that me?

109
00:09:17,370 --> 00:09:18,560
Hsieh Tien-ti.

110
00:09:20,490 --> 00:09:21,460
Just now...

111
00:09:23,000 --> 00:09:24,850
Was I the one who was lying on the ground

112
00:09:24,930 --> 00:09:26,830
and bleeding profusely?

113
00:09:28,280 --> 00:09:29,690
I saw you too.

114
00:09:31,270 --> 00:09:32,500
Did I die?

115
00:09:34,480 --> 00:09:36,020
You saw the Reflection of Time?

116
00:09:37,690 --> 00:09:40,910
Reflection of time? What's that?

117
00:09:41,830 --> 00:09:43,500
That's none of your business.

118
00:09:43,940 --> 00:09:45,310
Give me back my comb.

119
00:09:46,230 --> 00:09:47,110
Comb?

120
00:09:47,200 --> 00:09:48,080
Give it back.

121
00:09:48,430 --> 00:09:49,310
Give it back.

122
00:10:09,510 --> 00:10:16,020
♫ The crowd is big. I'm fading fast ♫

123
00:10:16,330 --> 00:10:21,300
♫ With just one look, you can save ♫

124
00:10:22,260 --> 00:10:25,260
♫ The prideful humans.
You're all-powerful ♫

125
00:10:25,340 --> 00:10:28,780
♫ But you've lost to time ♫

126
00:10:29,080 --> 00:10:34,500
♫ Where else can we go? ♫

127
00:10:35,070 --> 00:10:37,090
How many times have I told you?

128
00:10:37,180 --> 00:10:38,940
Watch where you're going.

129
00:10:39,640 --> 00:10:40,880
You bumbling fool.

130
00:10:41,800 --> 00:10:46,900
♫ Who says tomorrow will be bright? ♫

131
00:10:48,270 --> 00:10:51,570
♫ The rain will never end ♫

132
00:10:52,050 --> 00:10:53,330
Does it still hurt?

133
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:58,700
My name is 'Orad.

134
00:10:59,930 --> 00:11:01,340
From now on,

135
00:11:02,300 --> 00:11:04,330
I will be your guardian angel.

136
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:12,820
♫ When the souls come together,
I'm no longer afraid of regret ♫

137
00:11:13,520 --> 00:11:17,000
♫ If I went back to the beginning,
what would I choose? ♫

138
00:11:18,710 --> 00:11:23,070
You're 'Orad, my guardian angel?

139
00:11:31,690 --> 00:11:34,110
Why was she able to see
the Reflection of Time?

140
00:11:39,040 --> 00:11:40,320
Don't pretend everything is fine.

141
00:11:41,460 --> 00:11:42,390
Say something,

142
00:11:42,960 --> 00:11:43,710
Kakarayan.

143
00:11:48,330 --> 00:11:50,530
If you won't follow the path
I've prepared for you...

144
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:55,850
Why do you keep asking me
where to go next?

145
00:11:58,360 --> 00:11:59,940
Take care of it yourself.

146
00:12:00,070 --> 00:12:11,690
Take care of it yourself.

147
00:12:16,350 --> 00:12:17,190
You old geezer.

148
00:12:22,690 --> 00:12:25,280
I'll show you a magic trick.

149
00:12:25,860 --> 00:12:27,440
I'm starting to like you.

150
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:29,200
This will do.

151
00:12:31,220 --> 00:12:33,290
'Orad, where did you go yesterday?

152
00:12:33,380 --> 00:12:34,610
Why did you set me up?

153
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:36,280
I didn't set you up.
What are you talking about?

154
00:12:36,420 --> 00:12:37,380
Stop playing dumb.

155
00:12:38,090 --> 00:12:39,280
This isn't fair.

156
00:12:39,360 --> 00:12:40,020
I said I don't drink.

157
00:12:40,160 --> 00:12:41,430
Why did you make me drink?

158
00:12:41,870 --> 00:12:42,840
Yesterday, considering that

159
00:12:42,930 --> 00:12:44,560
we go way back,

160
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:46,270
I wanted to have a drink with you

161
00:12:46,580 --> 00:12:48,560
and help set your career straight.

162
00:12:48,650 --> 00:12:49,440
Calm down.

163
00:12:49,530 --> 00:12:51,550
Do you remember? You were so drunk
last night that you fell asleep.

164
00:12:51,680 --> 00:12:52,870
I even put a jacket on you.

165
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,500
And the important thing is

166
00:12:55,380 --> 00:12:58,590
you disappeared
in the middle of drinking last night.

167
00:12:58,860 --> 00:12:59,690
I disappeared?

168
00:13:00,570 --> 00:13:01,760
I even said,

169
00:13:02,460 --> 00:13:04,310
"I'll drink it if you can't."

170
00:13:04,400 --> 00:13:05,630
As I was about to make a toast,

171
00:13:06,820 --> 00:13:07,830
you disappeared.

172
00:13:08,540 --> 00:13:10,380
You said you wanted a drink,
but you're dozing off.

173
00:13:11,790 --> 00:13:13,510
You're an adult. Take care of yourself.

174
00:13:13,640 --> 00:13:15,090
Why did you drink
when you can't hold your liquor?

175
00:13:17,380 --> 00:13:18,570
Seriously.

176
00:13:19,710 --> 00:13:21,510
No matter how reluctant you are,

177
00:13:21,650 --> 00:13:22,260
as a Kawas,

178
00:13:22,350 --> 00:13:23,670
there's only one thing we can do.

179
00:13:24,420 --> 00:13:25,430
And that is to follow

180
00:13:25,520 --> 00:13:27,410
the instructions of mighty Kakarayan.

181
00:13:25,740 --> 00:13:30,750
♫ Come on, come on ♫

182
00:13:27,760 --> 00:13:29,210
Let go of all your regrets
about this world

183
00:13:29,300 --> 00:13:30,490
and leave.

184
00:13:30,840 --> 00:13:35,680
♫ Let me hear you ♫

185
00:13:33,660 --> 00:13:35,240
Forget it. It's no use talking about it.

186
00:13:35,810 --> 00:13:37,490
♫ Come on, come on ♫

187
00:13:37,570 --> 00:13:39,290
I'll drink it if you can't.

188
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:41,230
Here, cheers.

189
00:13:45,760 --> 00:13:46,770
I said I'd drink it,

190
00:13:46,860 --> 00:13:49,150
so you're really letting me
drink it alone.

191
00:13:49,230 --> 00:13:50,030
Fine.

192
00:13:50,990 --> 00:14:00,720
"Right at this moment,
show yourself to me."

193
00:14:00,850 --> 00:14:02,740
So that's why

194
00:14:02,830 --> 00:14:06,040
I appeared before her.

195
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:07,360
What are you mumbling about?

196
00:14:07,490 --> 00:14:09,300
Can you speak up?

197
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:11,190
Did you remember something?

198
00:14:11,280 --> 00:14:13,120
It's all your fault.

199
00:14:13,260 --> 00:14:15,370
That's why I did something so stupid.

200
00:14:15,500 --> 00:14:16,600
Something stupid?

201
00:14:16,690 --> 00:14:17,480
Wait.

202
00:14:18,540 --> 00:14:20,120
Tell me what you've done.

203
00:14:20,250 --> 00:14:22,500
This is a once-in-a-lifetime thing.

204
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,880
Let me hear it. It doesn't happen often.

205
00:14:28,390 --> 00:14:28,920
Well?

206
00:14:29,050 --> 00:14:29,980
I let Hsieh Tien-ti

207
00:14:30,060 --> 00:14:31,870
see something she shouldn't have.

208
00:14:32,620 --> 00:14:34,510
'Orad.

209
00:14:34,600 --> 00:14:37,320
I didn't know you had such a fetish.

210
00:14:37,460 --> 00:14:39,920
My goodness.
I guess I didn't know you very well.

211
00:14:40,840 --> 00:14:42,960
Which part did you show her?

212
00:14:43,090 --> 00:14:44,540
The front or the back?

213
00:14:44,630 --> 00:14:45,770
The Reflection of Time.

214
00:14:47,660 --> 00:14:50,040
Hang on, let me get this straight.

215
00:14:50,610 --> 00:14:51,490
What did you let the human see

216
00:14:51,580 --> 00:14:53,210
in the Reflection of Time?

217
00:14:55,320 --> 00:14:56,240
I showed her

218
00:14:56,380 --> 00:14:58,360
the Reflection of Time of her death
in the future.

219
00:15:02,540 --> 00:15:03,680
You let her...

220
00:15:04,250 --> 00:15:06,010
You let her see the climax?

221
00:15:06,100 --> 00:15:07,150
'Orad.

222
00:15:07,290 --> 00:15:08,870
My gosh.

223
00:15:10,060 --> 00:15:11,510
I mean

224
00:15:11,730 --> 00:15:13,400
it's you, 'Orad.

225
00:15:13,710 --> 00:15:15,120
The only messenger

226
00:15:15,250 --> 00:15:17,320
Kakarayan appointed in the human world.

227
00:15:17,630 --> 00:15:19,690
How could you have made such a mistake?

228
00:15:20,400 --> 00:15:21,410
It's all because of you.

229
00:15:21,940 --> 00:15:23,610
Stop blaming it on me.

230
00:15:23,700 --> 00:15:26,070
I didn't even know
where you went yesterday.

231
00:15:26,560 --> 00:15:27,790
You can't push the blame on me.

232
00:15:27,880 --> 00:15:28,450
I don't care.

233
00:15:28,800 --> 00:15:30,430
You have to help me clean up this mess.

234
00:15:31,840 --> 00:15:34,520
Okay, that's not hard to do.

235
00:15:34,610 --> 00:15:37,340
Here, let the god of wisdom teach you.

236
00:15:37,430 --> 00:15:38,350
Later,

237
00:15:38,480 --> 00:15:40,680
go to the Correction Bureau
and talk to my wife.

238
00:15:40,810 --> 00:15:42,660
Borrow the Comb of Memories from her.

239
00:15:42,750 --> 00:15:44,690
Then locate that Hsieh Tien-ti

240
00:15:44,770 --> 00:15:46,750
and wipe her memory clean.

241
00:15:46,840 --> 00:15:48,820
How could you not know what to...

242
00:15:50,710 --> 00:15:52,080
You're dead meat.

243
00:15:52,910 --> 00:16:07,870
[Mountain Travel, Get through 2021]

244
00:15:53,090 --> 00:15:54,100
Did I hear correctly?

245
00:15:54,190 --> 00:15:55,640
She wanted me, Wu Yi-han,

246
00:15:55,730 --> 00:15:56,830
the person she least trusts,

247
00:15:56,920 --> 00:15:58,110
to do the tour?

248
00:15:59,200 --> 00:16:01,620
Mom, are you kidding me?

249
00:16:01,710 --> 00:16:03,340
Did you eat something wrong?

250
00:16:04,970 --> 00:16:06,510
How many times have I told you?

251
00:16:06,600 --> 00:16:08,440
Don't call me "mom" at work.

252
00:16:08,530 --> 00:16:09,590
I'm telling you.

253
00:16:09,680 --> 00:16:12,010
There are only four people on this tour.

254
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:13,590
It's a group of good-looking Korean men.

255
00:16:13,680 --> 00:16:15,790
If you don't do a good job with it,

256
00:16:15,920 --> 00:16:17,070
I really don't know why I should keep you

257
00:16:17,160 --> 00:16:18,390
in this company.

258
00:16:20,150 --> 00:16:21,030
Tien-ti.

259
00:16:21,120 --> 00:16:22,130
Stop calling her.

260
00:16:22,220 --> 00:16:24,110
You always ask her to clean up your mess.

261
00:16:24,720 --> 00:16:26,880
Let me tell you something. Our Tien-ti

262
00:16:26,970 --> 00:16:28,950
has got bigger fish to fry.

263
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:31,410
You're different from her.

264
00:16:31,500 --> 00:16:34,230
Our Tien-ti

265
00:16:34,320 --> 00:16:35,550
is the fourth hitter.

266
00:16:36,080 --> 00:16:38,500
Number one, red card.

267
00:16:39,110 --> 00:16:40,340
Curry.

268
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:50,550
Tien-ti.

269
00:16:51,520 --> 00:16:52,440
Yes?

270
00:16:52,530 --> 00:16:53,850
Are you okay?

271
00:16:57,500 --> 00:16:59,570
I was thinking about work.

272
00:17:00,100 --> 00:17:01,510
I need to get something
from the meeting room.

273
00:17:01,810 --> 00:17:02,870
I'll be right back.

274
00:17:03,000 --> 00:17:03,880
Excuse me.

275
00:17:07,750 --> 00:17:09,290
Did I say something wrong?

276
00:17:09,380 --> 00:17:10,920
It was good.

277
00:17:11,010 --> 00:17:12,730
Maybe she likes LeBron James.

278
00:17:12,810 --> 00:17:13,869
Am I right?

279
00:17:13,960 --> 00:17:15,540
That's so weird.

280
00:17:15,630 --> 00:17:16,730
Logically speaking,

281
00:17:16,819 --> 00:17:18,530
unless you wanted her to see you

282
00:17:18,619 --> 00:17:19,589
and touch you,

283
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:21,790
she wouldn't have been able
to feel your presence.

284
00:17:21,920 --> 00:17:23,150
But you said that

285
00:17:23,069 --> 00:17:31,030
[Mountain Travel]

286
00:17:23,290 --> 00:17:25,220
not only can she see you,
but she can also touch you.

287
00:17:25,310 --> 00:17:26,500
She even traveled alone into the future

288
00:17:26,630 --> 00:17:28,040
and saw the Reflection of Time.

289
00:17:28,130 --> 00:17:29,930
That's impossible.

290
00:17:31,030 --> 00:17:32,170
Don't tell me
that you subconsciously wanted her

291
00:17:32,260 --> 00:17:33,800
to know you exist.

292
00:17:33,930 --> 00:17:34,810
That's why you purposely

293
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:36,270
let her see you and touch you.

294
00:17:35,740 --> 00:17:38,420
[Mountain Travel]

295
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,890
I got it right, didn't I?

296
00:17:37,980 --> 00:17:40,140
Do you think that's possible?

297
00:17:41,410 --> 00:17:42,070
I got it.

298
00:17:42,160 --> 00:17:43,350
It must be because you were drunk.

299
00:17:43,440 --> 00:17:44,410
So you lost control of your powers

300
00:17:44,490 --> 00:17:46,080
and got yourself in this mess.

301
00:17:51,180 --> 00:17:53,640
Stop talking about these things now.

302
00:17:53,730 --> 00:17:54,960
Let's just get the comb back

303
00:17:55,050 --> 00:17:56,680
and fix it.

304
00:17:56,770 --> 00:17:58,000
Then tidy up her memories.

305
00:17:58,090 --> 00:17:59,670
That's more important.

306
00:17:59,760 --> 00:18:00,820
You make it sound so easy.

307
00:18:00,900 --> 00:18:01,700
Don't you know

308
00:18:01,780 --> 00:18:03,280
that my wife is a control freak?

309
00:18:03,370 --> 00:18:05,350
If she finds out that you broke the comb,

310
00:18:05,440 --> 00:18:07,770
she'll kill you
and you'll perish without a body.

311
00:18:07,900 --> 00:18:08,780
I know.

312
00:18:08,870 --> 00:18:10,230
So I'll tell her

313
00:18:10,320 --> 00:18:12,480
that this is all your fault.

314
00:18:13,710 --> 00:18:14,720
How is this my fault?

315
00:18:14,810 --> 00:18:15,780
It's none of my business.

316
00:18:15,910 --> 00:18:16,740
It's totally your fault.

317
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:17,760
How is it my fault?

318
00:18:17,840 --> 00:18:19,300
I didn't do anything.

319
00:18:20,480 --> 00:18:21,580
That's so lame.

320
00:18:24,530 --> 00:18:25,850
Then let me ask you something.

321
00:18:26,070 --> 00:18:26,780
It worked?

322
00:18:26,860 --> 00:18:27,390
Yes.

323
00:18:27,520 --> 00:18:28,360
Who forced me to drink?

324
00:18:28,490 --> 00:18:29,240
I didn't force you to drink.

325
00:18:29,330 --> 00:18:30,080
You didn't make me drink?

326
00:18:30,160 --> 00:18:30,690
I didn't make you drink.

327
00:18:30,780 --> 00:18:31,840
You didn't force me to drink

328
00:18:31,920 --> 00:18:32,760
-at the office?
-I'm a sharpshooter.

329
00:18:32,850 --> 00:18:33,510
You're a marksman.

330
00:18:33,600 --> 00:18:35,180
I didn't force you to drink. Stop talking.

331
00:18:39,840 --> 00:18:42,040
That day...

332
00:18:43,580 --> 00:18:46,840
Was that really me on the ground?

333
00:19:12,400 --> 00:19:13,500
It's okay.

334
00:19:13,590 --> 00:19:14,870
It was all a dream.

335
00:19:15,610 --> 00:19:16,850
It was just a dream.

336
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,970
No.

337
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:29,470
But if it was a dream,

338
00:19:29,560 --> 00:19:31,940
then why do I have this?

339
00:19:36,950 --> 00:19:40,120
And at that time,

340
00:19:40,430 --> 00:19:42,940
I was reminded of all the things

341
00:19:43,730 --> 00:19:46,060
that person and I went through.

342
00:19:48,170 --> 00:19:51,030
What is going on?

343
00:19:52,440 --> 00:19:53,360
Go ahead.

344
00:19:53,450 --> 00:19:54,160
Why?

345
00:19:54,240 --> 00:19:56,400
You'll blame me then, won't you?

346
00:19:56,490 --> 00:19:57,720
It's because of you.

347
00:19:57,810 --> 00:19:58,780
It was you.

348
00:20:03,090 --> 00:20:05,240
Why are you here?

349
00:20:07,000 --> 00:20:08,240
She can see you.

350
00:20:08,320 --> 00:20:10,170
Who are you?

351
00:20:11,010 --> 00:20:12,200
You can see me too?

352
00:20:12,330 --> 00:20:14,000
Lower your voice. You're scaring her.

353
00:20:14,130 --> 00:20:15,540
Who's going to hear us?

354
00:20:15,630 --> 00:20:16,420
Calm down.

355
00:20:16,510 --> 00:20:17,830
We're just getting our stuff.

356
00:20:17,960 --> 00:20:19,100
Yes, calm down.

357
00:20:19,190 --> 00:20:20,470
Just give me the comb.

358
00:20:23,280 --> 00:20:24,340
We're civilized.

359
00:20:24,470 --> 00:20:25,970
We're Kawas who can communicate.

360
00:20:26,060 --> 00:20:28,080
Come, hand it over.

361
00:20:28,210 --> 00:20:29,360
Come on.

362
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:31,510
I don't want to.

363
00:20:31,640 --> 00:20:32,610
Don't make us use force.

364
00:20:32,740 --> 00:20:34,810
Even I'm scared of myself
when I'm angry. Quickly!

365
00:20:34,900 --> 00:20:37,190
What are you doing?

366
00:20:37,320 --> 00:20:38,420
Give it to me!

367
00:20:38,550 --> 00:20:40,180
You're going to get me killed!

368
00:20:46,910 --> 00:20:47,880
Hsieh Tien-ti.

369
00:20:51,970 --> 00:20:53,110
That's strange.

370
00:20:53,600 --> 00:20:55,450
I just heard her voice.

371
00:20:55,530 --> 00:20:57,600
Hsieh Tien-ti.

372
00:21:03,230 --> 00:21:04,330
Hsieh Tien-ti.

373
00:21:13,050 --> 00:21:15,910
This place is...

374
00:21:16,480 --> 00:21:17,750
Who are you?

375
00:21:17,840 --> 00:21:19,820
Why are you in my house?

376
00:21:19,950 --> 00:21:21,230
You also went to my office.

377
00:21:21,320 --> 00:21:22,110
Where am I?

378
00:21:22,200 --> 00:21:23,120
How did we get here?

379
00:21:23,210 --> 00:21:24,750
'Orad, grab the comb!

380
00:21:24,840 --> 00:21:26,910
Hand over the comb now!

381
00:21:27,210 --> 00:21:28,530
Stop scaring her.

382
00:21:29,110 --> 00:21:30,210
Okay, I won't scare her.

383
00:21:30,340 --> 00:21:32,850
Don't tell me you're the Ox-Head
and Horse-Face.

384
00:21:32,980 --> 00:21:35,310
Or are you black and white impermanence?

385
00:21:35,400 --> 00:21:37,600
I must be in the underworld. I'm...

386
00:21:37,680 --> 00:21:38,300
I've gone to the underworld!

387
00:21:38,390 --> 00:21:39,580
Calm down.

388
00:21:39,710 --> 00:21:41,690
-Miss.
-I'm in the underworld.

389
00:21:41,780 --> 00:21:43,670
Miss, calm down!

390
00:21:43,760 --> 00:21:44,240
Calm down, everyone.

391
00:21:44,330 --> 00:21:44,900
Am I dead?

392
00:21:44,990 --> 00:21:46,260
No, miss. Calm down.

393
00:21:46,350 --> 00:21:48,110
Breathe.

394
00:21:51,190 --> 00:21:53,390
Okay, calm down, everyone.

395
00:21:53,480 --> 00:21:55,500
Let's start over.

396
00:21:56,430 --> 00:21:59,680
Hi, let me introduce myself.

397
00:21:59,770 --> 00:22:01,880
I'm Li Pu-hui, the god of wisdom.

398
00:22:01,970 --> 00:22:03,340
We're not the Ox-Head and Horse-Face.

399
00:22:03,470 --> 00:22:04,790
And we're not
black and white impermanence.

400
00:22:04,880 --> 00:22:06,240
I'm a professor.

401
00:22:06,720 --> 00:22:08,400
We're Kawas.

402
00:22:08,480 --> 00:22:10,240
K-a-w-a-s.

403
00:22:10,380 --> 00:22:12,710
Spirit of all beings.

404
00:22:14,380 --> 00:22:16,620
You guys are Kawas?

405
00:22:16,710 --> 00:22:17,640
That's right.

406
00:22:18,380 --> 00:22:20,190
Don't doubt us as Kawas.

407
00:22:20,280 --> 00:22:21,860
As for why we're here,

408
00:22:21,990 --> 00:22:22,830
it's simple.

409
00:22:23,140 --> 00:22:24,590
Because we can appear anywhere

410
00:22:24,680 --> 00:22:26,130
and wherever we please.

411
00:22:26,390 --> 00:22:28,330
Like teleportation.

412
00:22:28,460 --> 00:22:30,090
Teleportation?

413
00:22:30,180 --> 00:22:31,800
Now, you're confused.

414
00:22:31,940 --> 00:22:33,080
Where the heck am I?

415
00:22:33,170 --> 00:22:35,890
This place isn't the underworld. It's...

416
00:22:36,600 --> 00:22:38,310
It's his home.

417
00:22:38,400 --> 00:22:39,940
Allow me to introduce.

418
00:22:41,970 --> 00:22:43,150
Stand up.

419
00:22:45,350 --> 00:22:46,810
The Kawas before you

420
00:22:46,890 --> 00:22:48,210
is called 'Orad.

421
00:22:48,350 --> 00:22:50,330
He's the god of rain,

422
00:22:50,460 --> 00:22:52,090
as well as the only messenger

423
00:22:52,170 --> 00:22:53,630
of Kakarayan.

424
00:22:54,460 --> 00:22:55,250
He's cool.

425
00:22:56,130 --> 00:22:57,670
Kakarayan.

426
00:22:58,160 --> 00:22:59,130
Kakarayan.

427
00:22:59,480 --> 00:23:02,510
He's the beginning of the world,
the beginning of everything.

428
00:23:02,600 --> 00:23:05,240
He's the boss of all Kawas.

429
00:23:05,370 --> 00:23:07,880
The Creator, as you humans call it.

430
00:23:11,140 --> 00:23:12,020
It's okay.

431
00:23:12,110 --> 00:23:14,570
Don't panic or be scared.

432
00:23:14,660 --> 00:23:16,240
I know what you want to ask.

433
00:23:16,330 --> 00:23:17,430
We came to you

434
00:23:17,520 --> 00:23:20,510
because we want to take back what's ours.

435
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:21,390
It's a bother.

436
00:23:21,520 --> 00:23:23,900
Because 'Orad passed out
from drinking last night

437
00:23:23,990 --> 00:23:25,830
and accidentally leaked
your time of death.

438
00:23:25,920 --> 00:23:27,810
It has disrupted the order
of this entire reality.

439
00:23:27,900 --> 00:23:29,970
That's why he has to clean up the mess.

440
00:23:30,060 --> 00:23:31,770
So he went to my wife

441
00:23:31,860 --> 00:23:34,590
and borrowed a comb
that can tidy up memories.

442
00:23:35,690 --> 00:23:37,490
It's the one you're holding.

443
00:23:37,580 --> 00:23:39,690
But unfortunately, you broke it.

444
00:23:39,780 --> 00:23:44,140
A comb that can be used
to tidy up memories?

445
00:23:46,250 --> 00:23:47,700
What are you talking about?

446
00:23:48,540 --> 00:23:50,650
Okay. Simply put,

447
00:23:50,740 --> 00:23:51,920
because of you,

448
00:23:52,010 --> 00:23:54,650
'Orad is in a load of trouble.

449
00:23:54,740 --> 00:23:55,800
Including me.

450
00:23:55,880 --> 00:23:57,690
So there's only one thing
left for us to do,

451
00:23:57,820 --> 00:23:59,050
which is to keep an eye on you

452
00:23:59,140 --> 00:24:01,690
and make sure you die
the way Kakarayan has planned.

453
00:24:02,790 --> 00:24:03,760
Hand it over.

454
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:06,490
So the image I saw

455
00:24:07,980 --> 00:24:09,300
wasn't a dream.

456
00:24:10,760 --> 00:24:14,940
The person lying on the ground
was indeed me.

457
00:24:15,070 --> 00:24:17,090
I will die.

458
00:24:17,180 --> 00:24:19,070
Yes, that's right.

459
00:24:19,910 --> 00:24:21,580
According to my previous orders,

460
00:24:21,670 --> 00:24:22,860
let's see.

461
00:24:24,880 --> 00:24:25,720
I got it.

462
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:26,810
Next Monday,

463
00:24:26,950 --> 00:24:27,910
which is also the day

464
00:24:28,050 --> 00:24:29,850
the last rain will fall on earth,

465
00:24:29,980 --> 00:24:31,350
I have to get out of here.

466
00:24:31,430 --> 00:24:33,190
Unless something happens,

467
00:24:33,280 --> 00:24:34,690
that day will be the day you die.

468
00:24:34,780 --> 00:24:36,100
Do you understand?

469
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:39,490
It's like he said.

470
00:24:39,570 --> 00:24:41,820
It doesn't matter
if you understand or not.

471
00:24:43,270 --> 00:24:44,680
Give us back the comb.

472
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:47,050
And we'll let you go back
to your old life.

473
00:25:04,430 --> 00:25:06,060
It's all right now.

474
00:25:07,070 --> 00:25:09,540
So the things that I recalled

475
00:25:10,330 --> 00:25:12,090
really happened.

476
00:25:12,880 --> 00:25:14,640
You used this comb

477
00:25:14,730 --> 00:25:17,020
and erased my memory, that's why...

478
00:25:18,380 --> 00:25:19,970
I forgot about you.

479
00:25:21,950 --> 00:25:23,570
If I hadn't broken the comb,

480
00:25:23,700 --> 00:25:25,730
I would never have remembered.

481
00:25:27,310 --> 00:25:28,060
Wait.

482
00:25:29,160 --> 00:25:31,710
You remembered what happened
between you and 'Orad?

483
00:25:35,320 --> 00:25:38,620
Why didn't you share this with me?

484
00:25:39,190 --> 00:25:41,300
But aren't you my guardian angel?

485
00:25:42,230 --> 00:25:44,030
Then why are you trying to kill me?

486
00:25:44,160 --> 00:25:46,060
That's not important.

487
00:25:48,170 --> 00:25:49,800
You'll forget everything soon.

488
00:26:02,640 --> 00:26:04,180
Get some rest. I'm leaving.

489
00:26:04,270 --> 00:26:05,200
Hold on.

490
00:26:09,860 --> 00:26:11,090
You said

491
00:26:12,370 --> 00:26:14,300
that I'll forget everything soon.

492
00:26:14,390 --> 00:26:15,710
What do you mean?

493
00:26:18,920 --> 00:26:20,510
Don't tell me

494
00:26:21,210 --> 00:26:23,320
you're going to use that weird comb

495
00:26:23,410 --> 00:26:25,130
to make me forget it all again.

496
00:26:26,970 --> 00:26:27,590
What else then?

497
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:29,830
What kind of nonsense is this?

498
00:26:32,390 --> 00:26:34,060
Don't you know what's going on?

499
00:26:34,410 --> 00:26:36,790
I'm going to die.

500
00:26:36,870 --> 00:26:38,680
Aren't you my guardian angel?

501
00:26:38,770 --> 00:26:40,700
How can you be so irresponsible?

502
00:26:42,420 --> 00:26:43,830
I'm irresponsible?

503
00:26:43,960 --> 00:26:45,500
What do you think?

504
00:26:46,250 --> 00:26:48,530
Who else could I be talking about
if not you?

505
00:26:49,020 --> 00:26:50,510
If you made me realize

506
00:26:50,600 --> 00:26:51,830
that all of this is true

507
00:26:51,970 --> 00:26:52,890
and what just happened

508
00:26:52,980 --> 00:26:54,170
is also true,

509
00:26:54,250 --> 00:26:56,100
you'd better not try and send me away

510
00:26:56,230 --> 00:26:57,690
with a mere few words?

511
00:27:00,630 --> 00:27:03,490
My faith has gone to waste.

512
00:27:03,800 --> 00:27:06,710
On every lunar calendar celebration,

513
00:27:06,790 --> 00:27:09,040
Christmas, Thanksgiving, and whatnot,

514
00:27:09,130 --> 00:27:12,430
I would pray devoutly
to everything I could.

515
00:27:12,510 --> 00:27:13,480
What kind of god are you?

516
00:27:13,570 --> 00:27:15,150
Why are you doing this to me?

517
00:27:15,990 --> 00:27:16,560
What?

518
00:27:16,820 --> 00:27:17,790
Shut your mouth!

519
00:27:27,030 --> 00:27:28,090
Do you know?

520
00:27:29,360 --> 00:27:32,050
In the memories that you brought back,

521
00:27:33,540 --> 00:27:35,740
you told me yourself.

522
00:27:36,930 --> 00:27:40,500
"From now on,
I will be your guardian angel."

523
00:27:43,930 --> 00:27:45,820
In that case,

524
00:27:45,910 --> 00:27:49,080
do your job as my guardian angel.

525
00:27:49,160 --> 00:27:50,920
How did it turn out like this?

526
00:27:51,980 --> 00:27:53,830
Not only did you not protect me,

527
00:27:53,960 --> 00:27:56,120
but you're also telling me to die.

528
00:27:58,710 --> 00:27:59,860
I'm really...

529
00:27:59,940 --> 00:28:01,000
The more I talk about it,
the angrier I get.

530
00:28:01,090 --> 00:28:02,320
Guardian angel?

531
00:28:02,410 --> 00:28:04,170
What kind of guardian angel are you?

532
00:28:04,300 --> 00:28:07,250
You only know to tell me to die.

533
00:28:07,380 --> 00:28:10,500
You're not helping a person in need.
This is murder!

534
00:28:10,590 --> 00:28:13,230
Are you crazy or what?

535
00:28:15,780 --> 00:28:18,330
Do you know what you're saying?

536
00:28:26,340 --> 00:28:29,550
How would I know what I'm talking about?

537
00:28:39,230 --> 00:28:40,640
What the heck?

538
00:28:43,020 --> 00:28:45,220
I only found out today

539
00:28:47,370 --> 00:28:49,750
that my life is a lie.

540
00:28:50,760 --> 00:28:54,240
My parents left me when I was young.

541
00:28:54,330 --> 00:28:56,310
My only family

542
00:28:56,390 --> 00:28:57,890
didn't want me.

543
00:28:57,980 --> 00:28:59,340
Without any explanation,

544
00:28:59,430 --> 00:29:01,940
I was sent away.

545
00:29:03,960 --> 00:29:08,270
I kept telling myself

546
00:29:08,360 --> 00:29:11,530
that I'm actually lucky.

547
00:29:11,620 --> 00:29:12,720
Compared to others,

548
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:15,710
I'm much luckier.

549
00:29:17,820 --> 00:29:19,980
Because I always believed

550
00:29:21,910 --> 00:29:24,460
even if no one else can see it,

551
00:29:25,560 --> 00:29:27,760
there must be a guardian angel

552
00:29:27,850 --> 00:29:30,890
who is quietly protecting me.

553
00:29:36,040 --> 00:29:37,400
Who knew that the guardian angel

554
00:29:37,530 --> 00:29:40,000
wasn't a guardian angel at all.

555
00:29:41,360 --> 00:29:42,640
In the end,

556
00:29:43,300 --> 00:29:46,020
you stayed by my side not to protect me.

557
00:29:48,360 --> 00:29:50,950
You just wanted to make sure

558
00:29:51,080 --> 00:29:53,420
that I would die
according to the time and place

559
00:29:53,500 --> 00:29:56,060
that you guys have planned.

560
00:30:07,980 --> 00:30:09,960
If I had known,

561
00:30:11,060 --> 00:30:12,690
I'd rather start off

562
00:30:14,050 --> 00:30:16,070
not having a guardian angel.

563
00:30:18,010 --> 00:30:20,300
I wish you had told me from the beginning

564
00:30:20,390 --> 00:30:21,620
that I'll die mysteriously

565
00:30:21,710 --> 00:30:23,950
in the near future.

566
00:30:24,920 --> 00:30:27,510
Then I wouldn't have had
to live like this.

567
00:30:27,600 --> 00:30:29,360
Having to constantly tell myself

568
00:30:29,450 --> 00:30:33,720
that I'm luckier than other people.

569
00:30:33,810 --> 00:30:35,610
I've been like an idiot.

570
00:30:40,230 --> 00:30:42,300
I think I owe you an apology.

571
00:30:44,540 --> 00:30:46,520
But in the world of Kawas,

572
00:30:48,850 --> 00:30:49,820
there is no sorry.

573
00:31:17,010 --> 00:31:19,210
[Hello? Hsieh Tien-ti, where did you go?]

574
00:31:19,300 --> 00:31:21,280
[Weren't you in the meeting room?]

575
00:31:23,570 --> 00:31:24,670
I'm at home.

576
00:31:24,800 --> 00:31:25,550
[You're at home?]

577
00:31:26,820 --> 00:31:28,100
[Weren't you in the meeting room?]

578
00:31:28,190 --> 00:31:29,600
[How can you be at home?]

579
00:31:30,780 --> 00:31:32,460
[Fali emphasized again and again]

580
00:31:32,540 --> 00:31:34,080
for you to be careful with the comb

581
00:31:34,170 --> 00:31:35,320
and not to break it.

582
00:31:35,400 --> 00:31:36,810
Otherwise, there will be
serious consequences.

583
00:31:36,990 --> 00:31:38,440
But you ended up breaking it

584
00:31:38,570 --> 00:31:39,580
and now, you came back to ask me

585
00:31:39,670 --> 00:31:41,390
when I'll be able to fix it?

586
00:31:41,520 --> 00:31:42,660
Don't you have anything else to say?

587
00:31:42,800 --> 00:31:43,500
Yes.

588
00:31:45,700 --> 00:31:47,150
I have a question to ask you.

589
00:31:49,220 --> 00:31:50,580
You once said

590
00:31:50,940 --> 00:31:53,000
that no matter
which Comb of Memories is used,

591
00:31:53,090 --> 00:31:54,460
any person whose memory was erased

592
00:31:54,540 --> 00:31:56,170
could break the comb

593
00:31:56,260 --> 00:31:58,680
and those memories that had been tidied up

594
00:31:58,770 --> 00:32:00,390
would return to that person.

595
00:32:01,850 --> 00:32:04,400
But why is it that after Hsieh Tien-ti
broke the comb,

596
00:32:05,280 --> 00:32:06,910
it didn't go as you said?

597
00:32:08,180 --> 00:32:10,120
'Orad, say no more.

598
00:32:10,210 --> 00:32:10,910
Fali.

599
00:32:11,000 --> 00:32:12,580
That's not what happened.

600
00:32:14,120 --> 00:32:15,220
Honey, calm down.

601
00:32:15,350 --> 00:32:16,370
Shut up.

602
00:32:17,030 --> 00:32:18,430
Kakarayan gave the bureau

603
00:32:18,570 --> 00:32:19,490
only a few days

604
00:32:19,580 --> 00:32:21,290
to evacuate all the Kawas.

605
00:32:21,470 --> 00:32:23,450
We're up to our necks in work,

606
00:32:23,630 --> 00:32:24,990
but you asked for a memory modification,

607
00:32:25,080 --> 00:32:26,310
adding onto our workload.

608
00:32:26,620 --> 00:32:27,760
Okay, that's fine.

609
00:32:27,850 --> 00:32:30,670
You're Kakarayan's
great messenger after all.

610
00:32:30,750 --> 00:32:31,680
In the shortest time possible,

611
00:32:31,810 --> 00:32:32,730
I got all the procedures done

612
00:32:32,820 --> 00:32:35,070
and gave you the Comb of Memories.
Now, look what happened.

613
00:32:35,240 --> 00:32:36,690
You broke the comb.

614
00:32:36,780 --> 00:32:37,750
Now, you're acting
as if everything is fine,

615
00:32:37,840 --> 00:32:38,760
asking us all these questions.

616
00:32:38,850 --> 00:32:39,950
Does this look fine to you?

617
00:32:40,790 --> 00:32:42,240
You're in the wrong, 'Orad.

618
00:32:42,330 --> 00:32:43,780
Tell them exactly what happened.

619
00:32:43,870 --> 00:32:45,270
Explain yourself.

620
00:32:45,360 --> 00:32:47,650
Rather than wasting time
listening to my explanation,

621
00:32:47,740 --> 00:32:50,160
you should get that comb fixed instead.

622
00:32:56,490 --> 00:32:59,130
Malusakadat, calm down.

623
00:32:59,220 --> 00:33:00,360
He's right.

624
00:33:00,760 --> 00:33:02,210
The most important thing now

625
00:33:02,300 --> 00:33:04,590
is how to handle this matter.

626
00:33:05,690 --> 00:33:07,710
I'll fix the Comb of Memories.

627
00:33:07,800 --> 00:33:09,870
As for what you mentioned

628
00:33:09,960 --> 00:33:11,540
about Hsieh Tien-ti's condition,

629
00:33:13,340 --> 00:33:15,280
people's memories

630
00:33:15,370 --> 00:33:16,860
are made up of past experiences
and emotions

631
00:33:16,950 --> 00:33:19,370
that are all intertwined together.

632
00:33:19,460 --> 00:33:22,190
Because of the experiences,
people become attached.

633
00:33:22,280 --> 00:33:23,990
And due to the emotional attachment,

634
00:33:24,120 --> 00:33:27,160
people find it hard
to forget past experiences.

635
00:33:28,260 --> 00:33:29,800
That's memory.

636
00:33:30,900 --> 00:33:32,970
The Comb of Memories can only brush away

637
00:33:33,100 --> 00:33:35,300
what people have gone through in the past.

638
00:33:35,960 --> 00:33:37,100
Because without experiences,

639
00:33:37,240 --> 00:33:39,220
a person's feelings have no basis.

640
00:33:39,520 --> 00:33:40,320
Naturally,

641
00:33:41,060 --> 00:33:42,870
people will completely forget

642
00:33:42,960 --> 00:33:44,760
the memories that have been brushed away.

643
00:33:46,520 --> 00:33:47,970
So you're saying

644
00:33:48,980 --> 00:33:51,670
Hsieh Tien-ti broke the Comb of Memories

645
00:33:52,330 --> 00:33:53,950
and recalled her experiences

646
00:33:55,190 --> 00:33:56,330
but not her feelings?

647
00:33:56,460 --> 00:33:57,210
That's right.

648
00:33:58,660 --> 00:34:01,870
But there's a possibility

649
00:34:01,960 --> 00:34:03,410
that she repeatedly looks back

650
00:34:03,500 --> 00:34:05,530
on the past experiences.

651
00:34:05,970 --> 00:34:07,950
And while doing so,

652
00:34:08,780 --> 00:34:10,409
she becomes emotionally attached
once more.

653
00:34:14,719 --> 00:34:16,480
I know you must be anxious

654
00:34:16,610 --> 00:34:19,250
in wanting to deal
with Hsieh Tien-ti's recovered memories.

655
00:34:19,389 --> 00:34:20,969
But as you can see,

656
00:34:21,060 --> 00:34:22,690
the whole Correction Bureau is busy

657
00:34:22,820 --> 00:34:25,150
with preparations
for the Kawas' evacuation.

658
00:34:25,989 --> 00:34:28,360
All the memory modification personnel

659
00:34:28,449 --> 00:34:30,429
are currently out on the field.

660
00:34:32,449 --> 00:34:33,820
I'm really sorry.

661
00:34:34,570 --> 00:34:35,840
We don't have an extra Comb of Memories

662
00:34:36,190 --> 00:34:38,000
to give to you.

663
00:34:38,480 --> 00:34:39,760
Please go back for now.

664
00:34:40,330 --> 00:34:42,620
We'll handle Hsieh Tien-ti's case.

665
00:34:43,150 --> 00:34:46,050
It's okay.
My negligence caused this problem.

666
00:34:46,139 --> 00:34:47,460
I'll take care of it.

667
00:34:47,980 --> 00:34:49,130
Let me know when it's fixed.

668
00:34:53,310 --> 00:34:54,360
Calm down.

669
00:34:54,449 --> 00:34:56,739
Fali, you're letting him go
just like that?

670
00:35:07,340 --> 00:35:08,400
[Hsieh Tien-ti.]

671
00:35:09,060 --> 00:35:10,820
You said you have a guardian angel

672
00:35:10,910 --> 00:35:12,710
who has been secretly protecting you.

673
00:35:13,370 --> 00:35:15,130
You finally met him yesterday.

674
00:35:16,010 --> 00:35:17,380
But he's taking you

675
00:35:19,050 --> 00:35:19,930
to die?

676
00:35:23,800 --> 00:35:24,680
That's right.

677
00:35:26,920 --> 00:35:29,210
At first, I couldn't accept it either.

678
00:35:30,050 --> 00:35:30,840
But it's true.

679
00:35:31,410 --> 00:35:32,640
It's like you said.

680
00:35:38,100 --> 00:35:39,460
You believe too much

681
00:35:39,600 --> 00:35:40,740
in this spiritual stuff.

682
00:35:40,870 --> 00:35:42,940
That's why you went off the rails.

683
00:35:43,030 --> 00:35:44,260
Maybe you could call
your guardian angel here

684
00:35:44,350 --> 00:35:45,620
and show him to me.

685
00:35:46,460 --> 00:35:47,780
Guardian angel.

686
00:35:47,910 --> 00:35:48,530
Guardian...

687
00:35:55,040 --> 00:35:57,460
Stop it.

688
00:35:59,610 --> 00:36:02,830
Fine, if you don't believe me,

689
00:36:03,530 --> 00:36:04,230
then tell me.

690
00:36:04,760 --> 00:36:06,430
How did I suddenly show up here

691
00:36:06,520 --> 00:36:08,020
when I was at the office?

692
00:36:08,110 --> 00:36:08,990
How did I get back?

693
00:36:09,070 --> 00:36:10,090
How did it happen?

694
00:36:10,660 --> 00:36:14,090
It takes half an hour
to get home from the office.

695
00:36:14,750 --> 00:36:16,910
From the moment you left
to the moment I called you,

696
00:36:17,040 --> 00:36:18,530
it was only ten minutes.

697
00:36:20,600 --> 00:36:21,700
Wait.

698
00:36:22,140 --> 00:36:23,330
Are you sure that you were already home

699
00:36:23,420 --> 00:36:24,470
when I called?

700
00:36:24,780 --> 00:36:27,770
Wu Yi-han, you're so stubborn.

701
00:36:28,170 --> 00:36:29,750
I told you everything in detail.

702
00:36:29,890 --> 00:36:32,170
You still don't believe me?

703
00:36:34,730 --> 00:36:36,000
Or maybe

704
00:36:36,090 --> 00:36:39,920
you can give me a more realistic solution.

705
00:36:54,170 --> 00:36:56,900
Something more realistic?

706
00:36:56,990 --> 00:36:58,530
I have an idea.

707
00:36:58,620 --> 00:36:59,940
Hsieh Tien-ti.

708
00:37:00,020 --> 00:37:02,580
Are you really going to look
for the Crown Prince of Lan Hua?

709
00:37:02,660 --> 00:37:03,980
That's obviously a scam.

710
00:37:04,950 --> 00:37:05,920
Don't be rude.

711
00:37:06,840 --> 00:37:08,120
There are many believers.

712
00:37:08,430 --> 00:37:09,790
Whether it's yin or yang,

713
00:37:09,880 --> 00:37:11,290
or something dirty,

714
00:37:11,420 --> 00:37:12,260
he just has to do this...

715
00:37:13,880 --> 00:37:14,980
Let it rip!

716
00:37:15,070 --> 00:37:16,220
That will solve everything.

717
00:37:16,570 --> 00:37:17,980
He's really good.

718
00:37:19,300 --> 00:37:20,130
Is he handsome?

719
00:37:23,700 --> 00:37:24,970
Hi.

720
00:37:26,380 --> 00:37:27,830
Hsieh Tien-ti.

721
00:37:27,920 --> 00:37:30,470
You said he was handsome.

722
00:37:31,220 --> 00:37:31,700
That's right.

723
00:37:31,790 --> 00:37:32,630
It's obviously a lie.

724
00:37:32,720 --> 00:37:33,510
I'm leaving.

725
00:37:34,120 --> 00:37:35,880
Don't be rude.

726
00:37:38,650 --> 00:37:40,940
-Your Highness, I want...
-Hush.

727
00:37:42,750 --> 00:37:44,240
It's okay.

728
00:37:44,330 --> 00:37:46,180
You don't have to tell me anything.

729
00:37:46,270 --> 00:37:47,450
I've seen everything.

730
00:37:48,160 --> 00:37:49,650
Miss.

731
00:37:50,670 --> 00:37:51,990
Behind you,

732
00:37:52,120 --> 00:37:55,420
a filthy being that's not human
is following you.

733
00:37:56,390 --> 00:37:57,440
Filthy being?

734
00:37:57,530 --> 00:37:59,030
Yes.

735
00:37:59,110 --> 00:38:02,060
There's something dirty following me.

736
00:38:02,150 --> 00:38:04,130
Watch your mouth. How am I dirty?

737
00:38:04,220 --> 00:38:05,580
Wait.

738
00:38:07,170 --> 00:38:08,270
I heard him talking.

739
00:38:09,280 --> 00:38:10,600
Yes.

740
00:38:11,170 --> 00:38:12,310
Your Highness, did you hear

741
00:38:12,400 --> 00:38:13,850
what he said just now?

742
00:38:14,430 --> 00:38:15,390
He told me...

743
00:38:23,710 --> 00:38:26,170
Mom, I'm cold.

744
00:38:30,400 --> 00:38:33,870
Miss, the one following you around

745
00:38:33,960 --> 00:38:37,040
is the baby
you couldn't successfully deliver.

746
00:38:37,480 --> 00:38:39,900
It's known as a baby spirit.

747
00:38:40,250 --> 00:38:41,400
And...

748
00:38:41,480 --> 00:38:43,820
he's not an ordinary baby spirit.

749
00:38:44,210 --> 00:38:46,590
He's an enormous baby.

750
00:38:47,510 --> 00:38:48,300
From my divination,

751
00:38:48,390 --> 00:38:51,030
your karma is pretty bad.

752
00:38:51,120 --> 00:38:53,630
If you wish to get rid of the bad karma,

753
00:38:53,720 --> 00:38:55,960
I would say you need

754
00:38:56,090 --> 00:38:56,970
at least 100 boxes.

755
00:38:57,060 --> 00:39:00,620
Yes, 100 boxes of orchids.

756
00:39:01,020 --> 00:39:03,350
If 100 boxes are too hefty a sum...

757
00:39:03,440 --> 00:39:05,550
One hundred boxes?

758
00:39:07,180 --> 00:39:09,600
The big, filthy thing is right here.

759
00:39:09,690 --> 00:39:11,140
Yet you can't see him?

760
00:39:12,110 --> 00:39:14,530
How dare you call yourself a psychic!

761
00:39:14,620 --> 00:39:15,890
Miss...

762
00:39:16,380 --> 00:39:18,440
-How much did you scam me for?
-Let's talk nicely.

763
00:39:18,530 --> 00:39:20,120
It's fine if you prefer to take 50 boxes.

764
00:39:20,250 --> 00:39:24,780
You big liar!

765
00:39:26,140 --> 00:39:28,920
Hsieh Tien-ti, hold up.

766
00:39:29,000 --> 00:39:30,010
Hsieh Tien-ti.

767
00:39:30,100 --> 00:39:31,250
You almost strangled him to death.

768
00:39:31,330 --> 00:39:32,350
What else do you want?

769
00:39:32,430 --> 00:39:33,620
That was a mistake.

770
00:39:33,750 --> 00:39:34,680
Calm down, okay?

771
00:39:34,770 --> 00:39:36,310
Stop pulling me!

772
00:39:37,140 --> 00:39:38,200
Are you going to stand there

773
00:39:38,330 --> 00:39:40,350
and watch me die
at the crossroad next Monday?

774
00:39:41,630 --> 00:39:43,260
How can I stay calm?

775
00:39:46,870 --> 00:39:47,750
All right.

776
00:39:48,540 --> 00:39:49,810
I'll go with you.

777
00:39:50,960 --> 00:39:52,410
What's the name of the master

778
00:39:52,540 --> 00:39:53,690
you said just now?

779
00:39:58,090 --> 00:40:00,370
Ms. Tsai-yun.

780
00:40:05,960 --> 00:40:07,990
Have you been having nightmares lately?

781
00:40:10,360 --> 00:40:12,610
Yes, but they're actually...

782
00:40:12,690 --> 00:40:14,890
The man you met in your dream

783
00:40:15,290 --> 00:40:16,610
told you

784
00:40:17,180 --> 00:40:18,850
you were going to die soon

785
00:40:19,600 --> 00:40:22,240
and there was no way out of it.

786
00:40:24,090 --> 00:40:25,100
That's so accurate.

787
00:40:28,270 --> 00:40:30,380
Yes. Ma'am.

788
00:40:31,610 --> 00:40:34,120
Can you tell me what's going on?

789
00:40:35,220 --> 00:40:37,550
Because you know too much

790
00:40:37,640 --> 00:40:39,530
of what you shouldn't.

791
00:40:39,620 --> 00:40:42,130
That's why it has come to this.

792
00:40:44,060 --> 00:40:44,860
Then...

793
00:40:46,570 --> 00:40:48,240
please tell me.

794
00:40:48,330 --> 00:40:51,020
Is there a way for me to fix this?

795
00:40:52,910 --> 00:40:55,280
There's a way to fix it.

796
00:40:55,900 --> 00:40:56,780
Really?

797
00:41:02,190 --> 00:41:04,350
Take the east exit.

798
00:41:05,320 --> 00:41:06,680
Go along the sidewalk.

799
00:41:07,160 --> 00:41:09,630
Cross the street at the traffic light.

800
00:41:10,020 --> 00:41:12,840
Walk 20 steps to the west.

801
00:41:13,940 --> 00:41:15,880
You'll come to a street lamp.

802
00:41:16,490 --> 00:41:19,660
Circle the lamp three times
with your eyes closed.

803
00:41:20,190 --> 00:41:23,530
Then take 20 steps forward.

804
00:41:24,320 --> 00:41:25,160
What?

805
00:41:26,740 --> 00:41:27,530
That's it?

806
00:41:29,430 --> 00:41:32,370
You'll find the path
that you thought was a dead end

807
00:41:32,510 --> 00:41:34,310
is not what you had imagined.

808
00:41:37,260 --> 00:41:39,410
The road is alive, my dear.
